这是育婴室所遇到的最令人悲伤的情况之一，没人知道她是否能够走出这段痛苦。

114
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:22,480
The new day brings totally unexpected and devastating news.
新的一天带来了完全出乎意料的、令人痛心的消息。

115
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:32,800
Well this morning I've just arrived at the nursery to some very very sad news indeed.
今天早上，我来到育婴室时，得知了非常令人悲伤的消息。

116
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:36,800
All of the elephants have left their stables except for one.
所有的大象都离开了马厩，只有一只没有。

117
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:44,160
Little jippie very sadly and suddenly died overnight. At this stage nobody knows why
小吉皮在夜间突然去世了，目前没人知道原因。

118
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:50,960
but certainly myself the keepers and all the other elephants are feeling the loss of a very special little orphan.
不过，包括我、饲养员以及其他大象在内，都因为失去一个特别的小孤儿而感到非常难过。

119
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:57,760
It's terrible to think that the last time I saw jippie he was resting happily on my lap.
想到上次看到吉皮时，它正幸福地躺在我的腿上，真是令人难过。

120
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:05,360
Now he's gone. Obviously what everyone thought was just teething was far more complicated
现在它已经不在了。显然，大家以为只是长牙期的问题，其实情况要复杂得多。

121
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:11,520
but for the moment it's a complete mystery. Perhaps Edwin has some idea of what really happened.
目前这仍是一个完全未知的谜题。也许埃德温知道到底发生了什么。

122
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:19,280
Oh all the keepers were very sad everybody because jippie was the keepers favorite.
哦，所有的守护者都非常难过，因为吉皮是守护者最喜爱的动物。

123
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:27,760
The real problem started during the night after feeding his milk at nine. I discovered that the
真正的问题出现在九点喂完奶后的那个晚上。我发现……

124
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:34,800
trunk had started to be wet. It didn't take a long time before we discovered that the wetness
树干开始变得潮湿了。没过多久，我们就发现树干的潮湿处变成了泡沫状。当树干里出现泡沫时，就无路可逃了。

125
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:42,480
in the trunk was changing into foam. When one has got foam in the trunk there's no way out.
后备箱里变成了泡沫。当后备箱里充满泡沫后，就无路可逃了。

126
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:48,800
There's no way out you can save it. Before the vet could come jippie had just collapsed.
你根本无计可施，根本无法挽救它。在兽医能来之前，它就已经死了。

127
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:57,280
And nobody did not know what to say or what to do. It was just very quick.
没有人知道该说什么或做什么。一切发生得太快了。

128
00:13:57,280 --> 00:14:11,840
Well when he was with you very very gentle, do everybody like him. So everybody was sad or
当他待在你身边时，非常温柔，那么大家都喜欢他吗？所以大家都很悲伤。

129
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:19,680
they keep all over sad. Everybody in their compound. No matter how hard everyone tries
他们一直都处于悲伤状态。他们所在的地方的每个人都是如此。无论人们如何努力。

130
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:24,800
fragile little babies like jippie are always at risk during these dangerous early years.
像吉皮这样脆弱的小婴儿，在那些危险的早期阶段总是处于风险之中。

131
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:35,360
And the sad reality is that despite all the love and care they receive,
令人悲哀的现实是，尽管他们得到了所有的爱与关怀，

132
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:43,120
the tragedy that befell jippie could happen to any one of them at any time.
吉皮所遭遇的悲剧随时可能发生在他们中的任何一个人身上。

133
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:54,160
At the new release site there's wonderful news. It's been several weeks since my last
新发布地点有好消息。距离我上次发布已经过了几周时间

134
00:14:54,160 --> 00:15:00,400
visit when rabies struck the herd and amazingly they all seem to have had an incredibly lucky escape.
当狂犬病袭击了那群动物时，他们似乎都非常幸运地逃过一劫。

135
00:15:04,160 --> 00:15:07,920
I've returned to see if their ordeal has left any lasting damage.
我回来查看他们的遭遇是否造成了任何长期伤害。

136
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:12,960
Looking around I can hardly believe the changes that have taken place to the landscape.
环顾四周，我几乎无法相信这里的景观发生了如此大的变化。

137
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:20,480
It's absolutely incredible what the rains have done to this place. I mean it's transformed.
雨水给这个地方带来的变化简直令人难以置信。它已经发生了巨大的变化。

138
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:25,200
It's like a different place. There's so much food now for the elephants they're going to love this.
这里就像另一个地方。现在有太多食物了，大象们一定会喜欢这里的。

139
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:29,920
Because up to now they've been struggling a little bit trying to browse, trying to get enough
因为到目前为止，它们在寻找食物时遇到了一些困难，需要从灌木丛中获取足够的植被。

140
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:35,600
vegetation from the bushes now they've got all this lovely lush grass.
现在则有了这片美丽的青草。

141
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:48,080
The thing I'm really noticing now is just how wonderfully well
我现在真正注意到的是，它究竟有多么出色

142
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,800
our elephants have settled in here at her thumber.
我们的大象已经在这里安顿下来了。

143
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:56,640
Because initially of course they didn't know this area at all and now they've got an established
因为最初他们根本不了解这个地区，现在他们有了固定的

144
00:15:56,640 --> 00:16:01,920
routine they're no longer nervous. Before it was just like a bunch of individuals everybody just
惯例，因此不再紧张了。以前就像一群人，每个人都在做

145
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:08,160
doing their own thing. Now there's a sense of real cohesion and they're acting to me just like
自己的事。现在则有了真正的凝聚力，他们的行为也就像

146
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:15,120
wild elephants. They're doing everything I would expect. Better still like a wild herd one of the
野生大象。它们正在做我预期会做的事。更理想的情况是，像一群野生大象那样，其中有一只年长的孤儿象成为族长。这正是大家所期望的。

147
00:16:15,120 --> 00:16:21,920
older orphans is now emerging as the matriarch. This is what everyone has been hoping for.
年长的孤儿现在正逐渐成为族长。这正是所有人所期望的。

148
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:26,640
All four of our larger elephants have got particular aspects of their characters that the little ones
我们四只体型较大的大象都具有一些独特的性格特点，而小象则没有这些特点

149
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:33,680
respond to but of all four of them it's Yata the most independent one that to me seems as if she is
在四个人中，最独立的是Yata，在我看来她似乎是最独立的。

150
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:40,800
possibly the matriarch. She's not the biggest here but she is the one that the others defer to
可能是族长。她不是这里最强大的，但其他人都会听从她的命令。

151
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:47,520
and when the herd moves on it's often Yata that drifts to the back protecting the young ones
当群体移动时，通常是雅塔会游到后面保护幼崽，并引导它们前进。

152
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:54,320
and encouraging them along.
它也在鼓励它们继续前进。

153
00:16:54,320 --> 00:17:00,640
It's not just the herd that's been transformed.
不仅仅是群体本身发生了变化。

154
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:07,520
The dried up waterholes are now full to overflowing and for these little alleys
干涸的水坑现在都装满了水，而这些小通道……

155
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:14,080
this is just heaven. You can just feel the sense of excitement with these alleys as they get near
简直就是天堂。当这些通道靠近时，你能感受到那种兴奋感。

156
00:17:14,080 --> 00:17:20,960
water. I mean they just know they're about to have a great time just splashing around.
水。他们的意思是，他们知道自己即将享受一段愉快的时光，尽情地嬉戏玩耍。

157
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:40,080
Just look at Makasha having the time of his life and this is where you see the changing moods
看看马卡沙正在享受着极好的时光，而这就是你看到情绪变化的地方。

158
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:44,960
of the elephants. I mean they are really enjoying themselves. I mean you can hear just splash of
那些大象们。我的意思是，它们真的玩得非常开心。你可以听到“扑通”的声音。

159
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:50,400
throwing water everywhere because for months they haven't had an opportunity like this and boy are
他们把水洒得到处都是，因为几个月来他们都没有过这样的机会，他们真是在弥补失去的时间。

160
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:53,680
they making up for lost time.
他们正在弥补失去的时间。

161
00:17:53,680 --> 00:18:03,280
It's been nearly eight months since our elephants arrived here from boy in Nairobi and what an
从我们的大象从内罗毕出发来到这里已经近八个月了，真是令人惊叹。

162
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:08,000
adventure it's been just getting them in getting them into the trucks and of course having them
这次冒险只是把他们弄进卡车里，当然还要把他们安置好

163
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:13,440
settle into what is a totally different environment for them and then there was an awful scare with
他们进入了一个完全不同的环境，随后就发生了可怕的恐慌。

164
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:19,280
rabies they just look at them now on their acting naturally on they having fun haven't they settled in
他们现在只是看着它们，仿佛在自然地表演，享受着乐趣，难道它们已经适应了吗？

165
00:18:19,280 --> 00:18:27,360
well. After all they've been through this must now seem like paradise. There's no doubt in my mind
嗯。毕竟它们经历了这些，现在肯定觉得这里像天堂一样了。我毫不怀疑。

166
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:32,960
that if Thumba is very much now then you home and of course it's that one vital step to them back to
如果图姆巴现在状态很好，那么你就能回家了，这当然也是他们重返自由的关键一步。

167
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:43,520
the wild. At last I'm full of hope for their future it's now down to them.
最终，我对他们的未来充满了希望，现在就看他们自己了。

168
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:50,880
So it's time for me to say farewell and head south to see how Emily's heard her getting on.
所以，是时候让我告别了，前往南方，看看艾米丽的情况如何。

169
00:18:55,280 --> 00:19:05,120
And from what I hear there have been major changes there too.
据我所知，那里也发生了重大变化。

170
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:18,560
Emily now spends every night outside the stockade but she still often meets up with the other
现在艾米丽每晚都待在栅栏外，但她仍然经常与其他人见面。

171
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:27,120
orphans in the park during the day. All year I've been waiting to see if Emily will take her last step
白天时公园里没有孤儿。一整年我都在等待，看看艾米丽是否会迈出最后一步

172
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:35,600
back into the wild. Now it seems as if she may have finally made her decision. Emily was just
重新回归自然。现在看来，她可能终于做出了决定。艾米丽只是……

173
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:42,960
weeks old when she was rescued and it's taken 11 years of hard work and heartache to get her to
她在被救时已经几周大了，而让她康复需要11年的努力与痛苦。

174
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:56,480
this point. It seems she's reached the end of her journey and for the younger Elies it's time to say
就在这点上。看起来她已经走完了自己的旅程，对于年轻的埃利斯们来说，是时候向他们心爱的母亲说再见了。

175
00:19:56,480 --> 00:20:00,320
goodbye to their beloved matriarch.
向他们心爱的祖母告别。

176
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:16,240
This is what this whole project is about helping baby orphan elephants to return to the wild
整个项目的目的就是帮助那些孤儿象幼崽回归野外生活。

177
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:21,040
in their own time and on their own terms.
它们可以按照自己的节奏，在合适的时间实现这一目标。

178
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:30,880
No one will ever be able to replace the family Emily lost but that was never the goal.
没有人能够取代艾米丽失去的家庭，但那从来不是目标。

179
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:39,600
The aim was to help her start her own family back among the wild herds and now she has that chance.
目标是帮助她在野外群中重新建立自己的家庭，现在她有了这样的机会。

180
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:46,560
My only regret is that I may have missed the opportunity to say my own goodbyes to her.
我唯一的遗憾是，可能错过了向她告别的机会。

181
00:20:46,560 --> 00:20:49,680
She really was very special.
她真的非常特别。

182
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:59,760
I can't help hoping that she might still be somewhere nearby.
我不禁希望她可能还在附近某处。

183
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:10,240
So I've come to check out her old herd just in case she makes one last appearance.
所以我来查看她的旧群，就怕她会再出现一次。

184
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:16,320
What do you mean look? I see between the trees there.
你说的“看”是什么意思？我在树间看到了什么。

185
00:21:16,320 --> 00:21:23,600
No the question is is it a wild elephant or is it a elephant they know
不，问题是那是野生大象还是那些人认识的大象。

186
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:30,880
just by the direction in which they're moving and the purposefulness says to me that whichever
从它们的移动方向以及其目的来看，我觉得它们会去检查一下。你知道可能是谁吗？

187
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:36,240
they're going to go and check it out. Any idea who it might be?
他们打算去查看一下。你知道那可能是谁吗？

188
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:46,560
Is it Emily? I'll tell you one thing I'm keeping this side of our elite stick and
是艾米丽吗？我告诉你一件事：我会保留我们精英团队中的这一方。

189
00:21:46,560 --> 00:21:50,320
act as a buffer whoever that elephant is don't want to make a mistake at this point.
不管那个“大象”是谁，都请他扮演缓冲角色，现在可不能犯错。

190
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:59,680
It's who? Edo and Edo is a bull. Was it an orphan?
那是谁？埃多……埃多可是个厉害人物。他是孤儿吗？

191
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:09,280
It was fantastic so maybe we'll get a wonderful sort of meeting. Listen they're talking already.
太棒了，也许我们会迎来一次美好的会面。看，他们已经在说话了。

192
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:21,440
Oh look there we've got one. Look Trump goes out. Who are you?
哦，看，我们这里有一个。看，特朗普走了。你是谁？

193
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:24,240
Do I know you? Yes I do.
我认识你吗？是的，我认识你。

194
00:22:24,240 --> 00:22:34,240
I mean that is a massive elephant. What is he? 14 years old? He's an adolescent. He's a teenager but
我的意思是，那可是一头巨大的大象。它是什么？14岁？它还是个青少年而已。

195
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:41,600
he is ginormous. But just look at these little ones. Look at the little balls the way he's their
它确实很大。不过看看这些小家伙吧。看看那些小球，它那样做……

196
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:45,120
hero right now and they are determined not to let him out of their sight.
英雄此刻就在那里，他们决心不让他离开他们的视线。

197
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:58,000
And this hopefully is the path that all of these orphans will follow back into the
希望所有这些孤儿都会沿着这条道路回到……

198
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:04,000
world. He's living life on his own terms in one of the most spectacular places in Africa
他正在非洲最壮观的地方按照自己的方式生活。

199
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:12,240
and doesn't that just say everything? A success story I reckon so.
这不就是说明了一切吗？我认为这真是一个成功的故事。

200
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:19,120
Even though I've failed to find Emily I have found one of her old orphan friends living wild
尽管我没能找到艾米丽，但我找到了她曾经的孤儿朋友之一，他们依然过着自由自在的生活。

201
00:23:19,840 --> 00:23:25,920
but it would still mean so much to me if I could see her enjoying her new found freedom before I have
但如果能在我离开之前看到她享受着新获得的自由，那对我来说意义重大。

